# Error Management, Swallow Elimination, SplitDB Persistence & CLI Inspector Specification
# Directory: 02-spec/21-app/04-vision-system-and-error-management-instructions/03-error-management-and-splitdb-spec.md
# Status: Approved Architectural Contract

## 1. Executive Summary & Problem Formulation

In industrial computer vision and Human-Machine Interface (HMI) applications, silent error handling and unmonitored exceptions pose catastrophic operational risks. When an error is caught and discarded or replaced with a fake fallback value (such as `[]`, `null`, or `false`), the application enters an unverified, divergent runtime state. Operators see misleading empty dashboards, hardware device locks remain unresolved, and diagnostic root cause analysis becomes impossible.

This specification establishes an uncompromising architectural standard for eliminating error swallowing across the entire **CAT Vision (CAT iVISION)** codebase, introducing a dedicated **SplitDB Error Persistence Database (`data/errors.db`)**, standardizing typed `Result<T, AppError>` envelopes, and delivering an interactive **CLI Error Inspector (`cat-cli errors`)** for rapid diagnostics.

```mermaid
flowchart TD
    subgraph UI_And_Stores["Frontend UI & State Stores"]
        CP["CameraPreview.tsx\n(Hardware Stream Acquisition)"]
        RS["run-store.ts\n(Inspection Run Execution)"]
