## 6. CLI Error Inspector (`cat-cli errors`)

To ensure developers and automated agents can inspect and triage errors without opening a web browser or SQLite client, `cat-cli` exposes a dedicated `errors` command module (`BE/cli/common/errors_inspector.py`).

### 6.1 Command Reference

```bash
# 1. List recent errors in tabular format
cat-cli errors list --limit 25 --unresolved-only

# 2. Inspect an error with full colorized stack trace and breadcrumbs
cat-cli errors inspect err-9f8e7d6c-5b4a-3210-fedc-ba9876543210

# 3. Stream real-time errors as they occur (tail -f)
cat-cli errors tail -n 10 -f

# 4. Mark an error as resolved
cat-cli errors resolve err-9f8e7d6c-5b4a-3210-fedc-ba9876543210
```

### 6.2 Inspection Output Format

```text
================================================================================
🔍 ERROR INSPECTOR: err-9f8e7d6c-5b4a-3210-fedc-ba9876543210
================================================================================
Timestamp   : 2026-10-31 02:40:03 UTC (1772412803)
Source      : web-ui
Severity    : ERROR [Code: E_CAMERA_STREAM_DENIED]
Status      : UNRESOLVED
Message     : NotAllowedError: Permission to access media device was denied

--- [ CONTEXT ] ----------------------------------------------------------------
Route       : /hmi/camera-setup
Camera ID   : daheng-usb-01
Browser     : Chrome 123.0

--- [ STEP-BY-STEP STACK TRACE ] ----------------------------------------------
 1. at CameraPreview.tsx:148:15 (CameraPreview.acquireStream)
 2. at CameraPreview.tsx:132:9  (useEffect.startStream)
 3. at react-dom.development.js:24456:12 (commitHookEffectListMount)

--- [ ATTACHED BREADCRUMBS (2) ] -----------------------------------------------
 [02:39:58] INFO    [navigation] Navigated to /hmi/camera-setup
 [02:40:02] INFO    [hardware]   Invoked navigator.mediaDevices.getUserMedia()
================================================================================
```

